    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green \u2014 **271 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe owner response DTO is generated from the OpenAPI spec by the openapi-generator Maven plugin, so the field is added in the spec and populated in the MapStruct mapper.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` response schema, alongside `id`/`pets`. It sits on `Owner` (not `OwnerFields`), so it appears only in responses, never as an input field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `displayName` on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n   Since `addOwner` returns `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, the create response now includes `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.createOwnerSuccess`** \u2014 added an assertion that `$.displayName` equals `\"Newman, George\"` for the created owner.",
